<h3>10. Run subagents in parallel</h3>
<p>A subagent is a separate agent the main session spawns like a deputy. Each one gets <strong>its own context window</strong> and reports only a summary back, which makes them ideal for read-heavy work like research and verification — what they read never burns your main context. Say "research 10+ references with parallel subagents" and several agents investigate different angles at once while the main session synthesizes. Being parallel, it also saves wall-clock time.</p>

